  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe optimization approach uses gradient descent with feasibility projection to minimize the maximum overlap integral C\u2085. Starting from the initial_h_values, we iteratively adjust h to reduce the maximum overlap while maintaining the constraints 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 and \u222bh = 1. The method computes gradients for the current maximum lag, applies a step, and projects back onto the feasible region.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n- Variables: h \u2208 [0,1]^{n_points}, sum(h) = n_points/2\n- Objective: Minimize C\u2085 = max_k \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx\n- Correlation computation: For each lag k, compute overlap length l_k=min(2,2+|k|)-max(0,|k|), scale by l_k\n- Constraints: 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1, sum(h) = n_points/2\n- Gradient: For active lag k, compute \u2207C\u2085 = 1/h_length * (1-h_shifted) - h_shifted derivative\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na. Initialize h with initial_h_values, compute feasibility projection\nb. Compute all lag correlations, find current max lag k and C\u2085\nc. Compute gradient for active lag k\nd. Perform line search to find optimal step size \u03b1\ne. Update h: h = project(h - \u03b1 * gradient)\nf. Repeat until time budget exhausted or convergence\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n- Start with \u03b1=0.1, vary by factor of 2 based on improvement\n- Perturb h randomly when no progress for 100 iterations\n- Use n_points=95 for computation speed\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n- Each iteration: 0.1s for gradient and update\n- Max iterations ~10^4 for 1100s budget\n- Include feasibility checks and C\u2085 calculation every 100 iterations\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n- Ensure h \u2208 [0,1] and sum(h)=n_points/2\n- Validate \u222bh=1 and check max correlation \u2264 C\u2085",
